<newsitem itemid="113888" id="root" date="1996-10-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Zinc Corp Sept qtr profit steady, sales up.</title>
<headline>Zinc Corp Sept qtr profit steady, sales up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-September versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit before capital spending  16.04 vs 16.29</p>
<p>    Capital spending/recoupment	    1.55 vs 0.29</p>
<p>    Zinc produced (tonnes)		 23,766 vs 25,309</p>
<p>    Zinc purchased (tonnes)		  nil  vs  nil</p>
<p>    Zinc sold (tonnes)		     27,496 vs 25,298</p>
<p>Full name: Zinc Corp of South Africa Ltd, managed by Gold</p>
<p>Fields of South Africa Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE - Zincor said domestic demand remained strong while 2,000 tonnes of metal were sold into the Far East in the quarter at a premium.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
